    <bpmn:process id="W_W481" name="W481. SEC Reportorial Requirements Compliance (GIS, AFS, MC 28)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual / quarterly SEC filing calendar due dates
Frequency: Annual (GIS, AFS); quarterly (MC 28 — material changes); event-driven (significant transactions)
Volume: 5 legal entities × annual filings = 25+ annual submissions; quarterly MC 28 as needed
Owner: Corporate Secretary
Participants: CFO, Controller, VP Legal, External Auditor, SEC
Source: workflow W481 — SEC Reportorial Requirements Compliance (GIS, AFS, MC 28)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W481_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W481_Lane1" name="Corporate Secretary">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W481_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W481_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W481_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W481_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W481_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W481_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W481_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W481_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W481_Lane2" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W481_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W481_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W481_Start4" name="Annual / quarterly SEC filing calendar due dates">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W481_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W481_Task5" name="Filing Calendar Maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Filing Calendar Maintenance: Corporate Secretary maintains the SEC filing calendar for all 5 entities: (a) GIS — due within 30 days from annual stockholders&#x27; meeting (W482), including the beneficial-ownership/affiliate disclosures the SEC requires within the GIS; (b) AFS — due within 120 days from fiscal year-end (or SEC-extended deadline); (c) MC 28 — within 30 days of any material change (officer changes, address changes, capital changes); (d) calendar alerts set 30 days, 14 days, and 3 days before each deadline
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 4 hours/annual setup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W481_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W481_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W481_Task6" name="Data Gathering">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Data Gathering: For each filing, Corporate Secretary coordinates with relevant departments: (a) GIS: HR provides updated list of officers, directors, and corporate secretary, and VP Legal provides the beneficial-ownership and affiliate disclosures required within the GIS; (b) AFS: Controller provides audited financial statements (after W9B year-end close and external audit completion W95/W351); (c) MC 28: Corporate Secretary identifies material changes from board resolutions (W124) and corporate events
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): CFO / VP Legal
Duration: 2–5 days/filing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W481_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W481_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W481_Task7" name="Document Preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Document Preparation: Corporate Secretary prepares filing documents: (a) complete SEC-required forms per entity; (b) attach supporting documents (financial statements, board resolutions, secretary&#x27;s certificate); (c) obtain required certifications (CPA certificate for AFS, notarization where required); (d) ensure consistency across all 5 entities&#x27; filings (e.g., common directors, intercompany disclosures in the AFS PAS 24 note and the GIS beneficial-ownership declaration)
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2–4 days/filing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W481_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W481_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W481_Task8" name="Internal Review &amp; Approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Internal Review &amp; Approval: CFO reviews AFS filing package; VP Legal reviews GIS and MC 28 filings; Controller verifies financial figures match audited statements; Corporate Secretary obtains board authorization where required
Responsible (R): CFO / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1–2 days/filing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W481_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W481_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W481_Task9" name="SEC Submission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: SEC Submission: Corporate Secretary submits filings via SEC Electronic Filing and Submission Tool (eFAST) or SEC Express Nationwide Submission (SENS): (a) upload completed forms and attachments; (b) pay filing fees per entity; (c) receive acknowledgment receipts and confirmation numbers
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 days/filing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W481_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W481_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W481_Task10" name="Confirmation &amp; Archiving">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Confirmation &amp; Archiving: Corporate Secretary downloads and archives SEC confirmation receipts; updates entity compliance files in document management system (W255); updates the entity master file with filing confirmation numbers and dates
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 hours/filing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W481_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W481_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W481_Task11" name="Deficiency Resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Deficiency Resolution: If SEC issues a Notice of Deficiency or Request for Additional Information: (a) Corporate Secretary coordinates with relevant departments to prepare response; (b) submits clarification or additional documents within SEC-prescribed timeframe (typically 10–15 working days)
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 1–5 days/response</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W481_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W481_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W481_Task12" name="Compliance Dashboard Update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Compliance Dashboard Update: Corporate Secretary updates the Corporate Compliance Dashboard: (a) mark each entity&#x27;s filing status as Filed, Pending, or Overdue; (b) archive all confirmation receipts; (c) generate annual compliance status report for Board review (W124)
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W481_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W481_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W481_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W481_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W481_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-289 (ensure controlled execution — GL &amp; Financial Close (PA-17.1).) | - operational: Corporate Secretary review and approval gate
Owner: Corporate Secretary</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W481_Assoc15" sourceRef="W481_Annotation14" targetRef="W481_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W481_Flow16" sourceRef="W481_Start4" targetRef="W481_Task5" />
