    <bpmn:process id="W_W482" name="W482. Annual Stockholders&#x27; Meeting (ASHM) Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual corporate calendar; typically held within 4–6 months after fiscal year-end, per Revised Corporation Code
Frequency: Annual (1 per entity); may hold joint meeting for parent + subsidiaries where permissible
Volume: 5 entities; typically consolidated into 1–2 meeting dates
Owner: Corporate Secretary
Participants: CEO, CFO, Board of Directors, Shareholders, External Auditor, VP Legal
Source: workflow W482 — Annual Stockholders&#x27; Meeting (ASHM) Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W482_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W482_Lane1" name="Corporate Secretary">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W482_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W482_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W482_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W482_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W482_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W482_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W482_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W482_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W482_Lane2" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W482_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W482_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W482_Start4" name="Annual corporate calendar; typically held within 4–6 months after fiscal year-end, per…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W482_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W482_Task5" name="Meeting Planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Meeting Planning: Corporate Secretary sets ASHM date(s) for all 5 entities, considering: (a) fiscal year-end close completion (W9B); (b) external audit completion (W95/W351); (c) SEC AFS filing deadline (120 days from year-end); (d) GIS filing deadline (30 days from ASHM); (e) director availability; (f) venue booking (or virtual meeting platform setup); coordinate meeting dates to maximize director attendance across entities
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W482_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W482_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W482_Task6" name="Notice &amp; Agenda Preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Notice &amp; Agenda Preparation: Corporate Secretary prepares and sends meeting notices to all stockholders: (a) written notice at least 21 days before meeting (per BuildRight by-laws); (b) include agenda, audited financial statements, director profiles (if election year), and proxy forms; (c) publish notice in newspaper of general circulation if required by by-laws; (d) prepare board books with supporting materials
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W482_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W482_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W482_Task7" name="Financial Statement Presentation Package">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Financial Statement Presentation Package: CFO and Controller prepare the financial presentation for stockholders: (a) consolidated financial highlights (revenue, EBITDA, net income); (b) segment performance by entity; (c) key financial ratios and KPIs; (d) capital expenditure summary (W21); (e) dividend proposal (if applicable, per W327)
Responsible (R): CFO
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W482_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W482_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W482_Task8" name="Pre-Meeting Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Pre-Meeting Coordination: Corporate Secretary coordinates logistics: (a) confirm quorum requirements per entity&#x27;s by-laws; (b) collect and validate proxy forms; (c) coordinate with External Auditor for auditor representation; (d) prepare voting sheets and election materials (if election year); (e) brief CEO and CFO on anticipated stockholder questions; (f) prepare draft meeting minutes template
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W482_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W482_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W482_Task9" name="Meeting Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Meeting Execution: Corporate Secretary convenes and manages the meeting: (a) call to order; establish quorum; (b) approve minutes of previous ASHM; (c) CEO presents operational highlights; (d) CFO presents financial results; (e) External Auditor presents audit opinion; (f) stockholder Q&amp;A; (g) voting on agenda items (financial statement approval, director election, auditor appointment, dividend declaration); (h) adjournment
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary / CEO
Accountable (A): Board Chair
Duration: 2–4 hours/entity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W482_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W482_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W482_Task10" name="Minutes Preparation &amp; Certification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Minutes Preparation &amp; Certification: Corporate Secretary prepares meeting minutes: (a) draft minutes within 5 working days; (b) circulate to attending directors for review; (c) finalize and certify; (d) archive certified minutes in document management system (W255)
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): VP Legal
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W482_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W482_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W482_Task11" name="Post-Meeting SEC Filings">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-Meeting SEC Filings: Corporate Secretary triggers SEC reportorial filings: (a) GIS filing within 30 days of ASHM (W481); (b) MC 28 filing if directors or officers changed at the meeting (W481); (c) SEC Form ADT (Address/ directors/ TIN) if any director changes
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Per W481</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W482_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W482_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W482_Task12" name="Action Item Follow-Up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Action Item Follow-Up: Corporate Secretary tracks post-ASHM action items: (a) dividend payment processing (if declared, per W327); (b) board committee reconstitution (if directors changed); (c) external auditor engagement letter (if appointed or re-appointed); (d) update corporate records and entity master file (W124)
Responsible (R): Corporate Secretary
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W482_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W482_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W482_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W482_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W482_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-289 (ensure controlled execution — GL &amp; Financial Close (PA-17.1).) | - operational: Corporate Secretary review and approval gate
Owner: Corporate Secretary</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W482_Assoc15" sourceRef="W482_Annotation14" targetRef="W482_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W482_Flow16" sourceRef="W482_Start4" targetRef="W482_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W482_Flow17" sourceRef="W482_Task5" targetRef="W482_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W482_Flow18" sourceRef="W482_Task6" targetRef="W482_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W482_Flow19" sourceRef="W482_Task7" targetRef="W482_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W482_Flow20" sourceRef="W482_Task8" targetRef="W482_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W482_Flow21" sourceRef="W482_Task9" targetRef="W482_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W482_Flow22" sourceRef="W482_Task10" targetRef="W482_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W482_Flow23" sourceRef="W482_Task11" targetRef="W482_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W482_Flow24" sourceRef="W482_Task12" targetRef="W482_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W482_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W482_plane" bpmnElement="W_W482">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W482_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W482_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="2000" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
