    <bpmn:process id="W_W877" name="W877. Product Recall Vendor Recovery &amp; Cost Reimbursement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Recall disposition complete (W875); financial impact quantified
Frequency: 3–5 vendor recovery processes per year
Volume: Average recovery claim: PHP 200,000–5,000,000 depending on product and recall scope
Owner: Procurement Manager / Finance Controller
Participants: Quality Manager, Finance Controller, Legal Counsel, Vendor Account Manager, Insurance Coordinator
Source: workflow W877 — Product Recall Vendor Recovery &amp; Cost Reimbursement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W877_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W877_Lane1" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W877_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W877_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W877_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W877_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W877_Lane2" name="Legal Counsel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W877_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W877_Lane3" name="Procurement Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W877_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W877_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W877_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W877_Start5" name="Recall disposition complete (W875); financial impact quantified">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W877_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W877_Task6" name="Compile recall cost documentation — aggregate all costs: (a) inventory value at…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Compile recall cost documentation — aggregate all costs: (a) inventory value at cost (destroyed or returned), (b) reverse logistics (return shipping, disposal), (c) customer refund cost, (d) customer service incremental cost, (e) regulatory compliance cost, (f) brand/marketing remediation cost, (g) business interruption (if product was top seller)
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): Procurement Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W877_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W877_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W877_Task7" name="Determine vendor liability — review: (a) vendor contract warranty/indemnity…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Determine vendor liability — review: (a) vendor contract warranty/indemnity clause, (b) product defect root cause (manufacturing vs. BuildRight handling), (c) vendor insurance coverage, (d) force majeure exclusions; Legal Counsel advises on contractual position
Responsible (R): Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): Procurement Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W877_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W877_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W877_Task8" name="Issue vendor recovery demand — send formal demand letter to vendor: cost…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Issue vendor recovery demand — send formal demand letter to vendor: cost breakdown, contractual basis for recovery, supporting documentation, and requested reimbursement timeline (30 days)
Responsible (R): Procurement Manager
Accountable (A): Legal Counsel
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W877_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W877_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W877_Task9" name="Negotiate settlement — vendor may: (a) accept full reimbursement via credit…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Negotiate settlement — vendor may: (a) accept full reimbursement via credit memo, (b) accept partial (dispute certain cost categories), (c) reject (claim force majeure or BuildRight fault); negotiate to resolution; for disputed claims &gt; PHP 1 million, engage Legal for mediation
Responsible (R): Procurement Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–20 hours (over 2–8 weeks)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W877_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W877_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W877_Task10" name="Process vendor credit memo — upon agreement, record vendor credit in AP module…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Process vendor credit memo — upon agreement, record vendor credit in AP module; offset against future invoices or request direct payment; post recovery to recall cost center
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W877_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W877_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W877_Task11" name="Insurance recovery coordination — if vendor recovery insufficient, coordinate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Insurance recovery coordination — if vendor recovery insufficient, coordinate with Insurance Coordinator for product liability or recall insurance claim (per W864); document unrecovered balance
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): Insurance Coordinator
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W877_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W877_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W877_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W877_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W877_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-289 (ensure controlled execution — GL &amp; Financial Close (PA-17.1).) | - operational: Procurement Manager / Finance Controller review and approval gate
Owner: Procurement Manager / Finance Controller</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
