    <bpmn:process id="W_W1431" name="W1431. Multi-Entity Fixed Asset Capitalization, Intercompany Asset Transfer &amp; Depreciation Consolidation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Asset purchase order completed (goods receipt + invoice per W7); or construction-in-progress project completed (new store/DC per W1427); or intercompany asset transfer (e.g., IT equipment transferred between entities); or month-end depreciation run
Frequency: Ongoing for capitalization (200+ store build-outs, equipment purchases); monthly depreciation run per entity; quarterly intercompany asset transfer reconciliation
Volume: ~10–15 new store build-outs/year (PHP 15–30M each per W276 = PHP 150–450M capex); ~600 POS terminal assets; ~4 DC equipment sets; ~3,000 IT assets; ~40 owned vehicles (rest 3PL-contracted); total fixed asset register: ~5,000–10,000 assets across 5 entities
Owner: Fixed Asset Accountant
Participants: Fixed Asset Accountant, Controller, DC Supervisor, IT Manager, VP Store Operations, Consolidation Accountant
Source: workflow W1431 — Multi-Entity Fixed Asset Capitalization, Intercompany Asset Transfer &amp; Depreciation Consolidation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1431_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1431_Lane1" name="Fixed Asset Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1431_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1431_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1431_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1431_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1431_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1431_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1431_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1431_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1431_Start4" name="Asset purchase order completed (goods receipt + invoice per W7); or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1431_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1431_Task5" name="Asset capitalization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Asset capitalization: When an asset is acquired or constructed: (a) Fixed Asset Accountant reviews AP invoice and goods receipt per W7: (i) verify the item meets capitalization threshold per BuildRight policy (typically PHP 10,000 minimum per item, lower for IT assets at PHP 5,000), (ii) classify asset: land, building, machinery, furniture/fixtures, IT equipment, vehicle, (iii) assign useful life per BIR-prescribed rates, (iv) assign to correct entity and location (store, DC, HQ), (b) system creates fixed asset master record: (i) asset number, description, serial number, (ii) cost, accumulated depreciation, net book value, (iii) entity, location, department, custodian, (iv) useful life, depreciation method (straight-line per Philippine standard), (v) capitalization date (date placed in service), (c) journal entry: Dr. Fixed Asset / Cr. AP or Cash or CIP (construction-in-progress)
Responsible (R): Fixed Asset Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 15–30 min/asset</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1431_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1431_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1431_Task6" name="Construction-in-progress (CIP) to fixed asset">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Construction-in-progress (CIP) to fixed asset: For large capital projects (new store build-outs per W1427): (a) during construction: costs accumulated in CIP account (Dr. CIP / Cr. AP/Cash), (b) upon project completion and certificate of occupancy: (i) Fixed Asset Accountant reviews all CIP costs: construction, fixtures, POS equipment, IT infrastructure, signage — verify all costs are capitalizable (exclude expensed items like pre-opening marketing, training costs), (ii) reclassify from CIP to appropriate fixed asset categories: building/leasehold improvements, fixtures, equipment, (iii) depreciation begins from the date the asset is placed in service (store opening date)
Responsible (R): Fixed Asset Accountant / VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 4–8 hours/project</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1431_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1431_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1431_Task7" name="Monthly depreciation run">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly depreciation run: (a) system runs monthly depreciation per entity: (i) straight-line depreciation per BIR useful life schedules, (ii) for newly capitalized assets: first month depreciation may be pro-rated based on days in service, (iii) for disposed assets: depreciation stops at disposal date, (b) journal entries per entity: Dr. Depreciation Expense / Cr. Accumulated Depreciation, (c) Fixed Asset Accountant reviews depreciation schedule: verify no assets with zero net book value still depreciating, verify new assets are depreciating correctly, (d) 5 entities × 1 depreciation run/month = 5 monthly depreciation journals
Responsible (R): System / Fixed Asset Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1431_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1431_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1431_Task8" name="Intercompany asset transfer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Intercompany asset transfer: When an asset transfers between entities (e.g., vehicle transferred from Holdings Inc. to Logistics Inc.): (a) Fixed Asset Accountant derecognizes asset in transferring entity: Dr. Accumulated Depreciation / Dr. IC Receivable (NBV) / Cr. Fixed Asset (cost), (b) recognizes asset in receiving entity: Dr. Fixed Asset (NBV) / Cr. IC Payable (NBV), (c) useful life reassessment: remaining useful life based on condition and remaining economic life, (d) IC settlement per W14, (e) in consolidation: IC receivable/payable eliminates; asset continues at original cost and accumulated depreciation (no step-up in basis)
Responsible (R): Fixed Asset Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1–2 hours/transfer</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1431_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1431_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1431_Task9" name="Annual fixed asset physical verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual fixed asset physical verification: (a) annually, Fixed Asset Accountant coordinates with Store Managers and DC Supervisors: (i) verify existence of high-value assets (POS terminals, forklifts, IT equipment) per location, (b) identify: (i) missing assets (possible theft or unrecorded disposal), (ii) assets at unexpected locations (unrecorded transfers), (iii) fully depreciated assets still in use (should remain on books) or disposed but not derecognized, (c) post adjustments: record disposals, transfers, write-offs
Responsible (R): Fixed Asset Accountant / Store Manager / DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 2–3 weeks/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1431_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1431_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1431_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1431_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1431_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-289 (ensure controlled execution — GL &amp; Financial Close (PA-17.1).) | - operational: Fixed Asset Accountant review and approval gate
Owner: Fixed Asset Accountant</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1431_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1431_Annotation11" targetRef="W1431_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
